  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Define \\( a\\clubsuit b=a^2b-ab^2 .\\) Which of the following describes the set of points \\( (x, y) \\) for which \\( x\\clubsuit y=y\\clubsuit x ?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "A finite set of points"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "One line"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "Two parallel lines"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "Two intersecting lines"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "Three lines"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2013-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The condition is \\(x\\clubsuit y=y\\clubsuit x\\), so \\(x^2y-xy^2=y^2x-yx^2\\).\n\nCombining like terms gives \\(2x^2y-2xy^2=2xy(x-y)=0\\).\n\nThus \\(x=0\\), \\(y=0\\), or \\(x=y\\). These are three lines.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E .",
